190: - **Changing config files referenced by `configUrls`** does NOT require rebuilding—just update the file and refresh the browser
191: 
192: This means you can update module configurations at runtime without rebuilding, as long as the config files are accessible via HTTP/HTTPS. 
193: 
194: **Configuration file structure:**
195: 
196: Each key in the config file corresponds to a frontend module name (e.g., `@openmrs/esm-patient-chart-app`). The value of each key is an object containing the configuration properties that you want to override for that module. These properties correspond to whatever properties are defined in the module's config schema.
197: 
198: **Example configuration file:**
199: 
200: ```json
201: {
202:   "@openmrs/esm-patient-chart-app": {
203:     "showRecommendedVisitTypeTab": true,
204:     "showAllEncountersTab": false
205:   },
206:   "@openmrs/esm-primary-navigation-app": {
207:     "logo": {
208:       "src": "${openmrsSpaBase}/assets/my-logo.svg",
209:       "alt": "My Organization Logo"
210:     }
211:   }
212: }
213: ```
